Package: spinet
Type: Package
Title: Spatial Interaction Networks Under Environmental Change
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ehsan", "Rahimi", email = "ehsanrahimi666@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Chuleui", "Jung", email = "cjung@gknu.ac.kr", role = "aut"))
Description: A raster-native framework for projecting ecological interaction
    networks through space and time from species distribution model output.
    The package couples per-species habitat suitability surfaces with an
    interaction constraint layer (a metaweb and/or trait-, phenology- and
    elevation-based forbidden-link rules) to construct spatially explicit
    interaction networks, and provides tools for network metrics, interaction
    beta-diversity partitioning sensu Poisot and others (2012)
    <doi:10.1111/ele.12002>, rewiring, coextinction robustness with rewiring
    sensu Vizentin-Bugoni and others (2020) <doi:10.1111/2041-210X.13306>,
    and factorial simulation experiments. All six interaction sign structures
    (mutualism, antagonism, commensalism, amensalism, competition,
    neutralism) are supported through a Relations Ontology-based interaction
    vocabulary compatible with Global Biotic Interactions. The package
    consumes species distribution model output; it does not fit
    distribution models.
